 <seg id="s0009" group="l0001" targets="p1" role="patient_specific">In the current study, we reported a patient with 
SPS whose nighttime dyspnea was successfully 
managed by the NIPPV application. To the best 
of our knowledge, this is the first study to show 
that NIPPV can be one of the useful therapeutic 
options for managing dyspnea induced by SPS.</seg> 
However, because this is a case report, our study 
is limited. Also, we still do not know when is the 
optimal time to start NIPPV treatment in patients 
with dyspnea after SPS. Further studies involving 
larger cases would be warranted for wide NIPPV 
application for controlling respiratory symptoms 
in patients with SPS. Also, studies for determining 
the optimal time to initiate NIPPV treatment 
should be conducted in the future.
